format:\r\nreminder_time = reminder_date_time.strftime('%B %d, %Y %I:%M:%S %p')\r\n\r\nCode:\r\n\r\n```\r\nUpdate the applescript_command with the corrected reminder_time:\r\napplescript_command = f\"\"\"\r\ntell application \"Reminders\"\r\n    tell list \"Reminders\"\r\n        make new reminder with properties {{name:\"Leave\", due date:date \"{reminder_time}\"}}\r\n    end tell\r\nend tell\r\n\"\"\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n### 4. Execute the Corrected Command:\r\nOnce you've fixed the date and time format in the AppleScript command, try running it again using osascript:\r\n\r\n`osascript -e \"$applescript_command\"`\r\n\r\n\r\nIf the command is correct, the reminder should be created successfully in your Reminders app.", "created_at": "2024-04-11T17:29:41Z"}
